# Board rotation controls and compact bottom labels

Add left/right quarter-turn controls to the Board and keep every bottom-bar label on one line.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The Board screen shows a circular-arrow-left action and a circular-arrow-right action.
- [ ] Tapping left rotates the board view 90 degrees counter-clockwise.
- [ ] Tapping right rotates the board view 90 degrees clockwise.
- [ ] Four repeated rotations in either direction return to the original orientation without cumulative geometry drift.
- [ ] Rotation applies consistently in view and edit modes, including terrain, numbers, roads, buildings, ghosts, and interaction targets.
- [ ] Rotation does not mutate the underlying logical board coordinates or saved board state.
- [ ] Existing pan, zoom, tap-to-focus, and hold/radial editing remain correct in every orientation.
- [ ] Edit, Hand, and Analysis bottom-bar labels use smaller fonts and fit comfortably on one line.
- [ ] Controls have distinct accessible labels and identifiers.
- [ ] Geometry/unit and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused rotation and compact-layout checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.
